// @name: Duration & Tempo
// @tagline: Note and group duration with ':' (e.g. {A B}:2, A4:1/2) and global tempo
// @language: bpscript
// @outputs: audio
// @level: intermediate
// @tags: basics
//
// Duration & Tempo — two distinct concepts
//
// DURATION is written with a GLUED ':' (it replaces the old [speed], removed 2026-06-26):
//   - on a group : {G4 A4 B4}:2   → the group fits inside polymetric frame 2
//   - on a note  : A4:1/2          → eighth note  (A4:1 = quarter, A4:2 = half)
// ⚠️ the ':' must be GLUED: `{...}:2`, `A4:1/2`. Spaced (`A4 1/2`) = old meaning (rest).
//
// TEMPO (the pace, the clock) is a SEPARATE concept: @tempo:72 (global).

@core
@alphabet.western:audio
@tempo:72

// Normal, then group at frame 2, then at frame 1/2, then per-note durations
S -> Normal Fast Slow Notes Final

Normal -> C4 D4 E4 F4
Fast   -> {G4 A4 B4 C5 B4 A4 G4 F4}:2
Slow   -> {E4 D4 C4}:1/2
Notes  -> C4:1 D4:1/2 E4:1/2 F4:2
Final  -> C4 _ _ _
